SUMMARY:Egypt Beyond the Pyramids: The Egypt Most Tourists Miss
DESCRIPTION:Most people picture pyramids when they think of Egypt. But it 
 also has the White Desert’s surreal rock formations\, the salt lakes of 
 Siwa Oasis\, a valley of whale fossils\, and modern landmarks like the 
 Bibliotheca Alexandrina. Whether you’re planning a trip or curious about 
 Egypt beyond the usual sights\, join us to discover a side that's often 
 overlooked. Presented by Jenny Montasir\, Montclair State professor and 
 founder of EgyptEd.
LOCATION:Bloomfield - Theater\, Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Special Event
UID:LibCal-10270-17628082
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17628082
END:VEVENT
