SUMMARY:Admission Possible: Applying to College
DESCRIPTION:*** This program is free to attend\, but you must register. 
 Teens and/or their Adults are welcome to attend . *** \n\nJoin us as we 
 learn all about the many factors that determine whether and where you get 
 into College.\n\nWe will also learn:\n\n\n	what influences and informs 
 Admissions Committees decisions\n	how to best present a strong student 
 application\n	how to create a suitable list of colleges that meet a 
 student's needs\n	insider info on the College Essay\n	how the Financial Aid 
 process works\n	Urban Myths about colleges\n\n\nThis program will be lead 
 by William "Bill" Indek. Bill has 36 years experience as a Guidance 
 Counselor at Glen Ridge High School. During the last 10 years there he 
 occupied  the position of Department Chairmen. In addition to that\, Bill 
 also:\n\n\n	served on the Middle States Evaluation Team  & Co-Chaired the 
 Essex County North West College Fair Committee.\n	was a Member and past 
 President of the Essex County Guidance Association\n	was a Member of the NJ 
 Association of College Admissions Counselors Association\n	was a Member of 
 the College Board\n	was recognized by the NJ Interscholastic Association in 
 2004 for mentoring & counseling student athletes. \n	has visited 586 
 colleges (really!)\n
LOCATION:Bloomfield - Board Room\, Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10270-17565649
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/bloomfield/college
END:VEVENT
