BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261015T140000Z
DTEND:20261015T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261015T000000Z
SUMMARY:Entrepreneurship Bootcamp
DESCRIPTION:*** This is a free program\, but you must register to attend. 
 \n\nemail: reference@bloomfield.bccls.org\n\ncall: 973-566-6200 ext. 215 
 ***\n\nThinking about starting a business—or wondering what it takes to 
 move your idea to the next level? This two-day introductory 
 entrepreneurship bootcamp provides a practical overview of the key areas 
 every new entrepreneur should understand.\n\nPresented by Jesse Bryant\, 
 Certified Business Consultant with the Small Business Administration 
 (SBA)\, SCORE\, and Veterans Business Outreach Center (VBOC)\, the program 
 will cover the fundamentals of building a business\, including financing 
 options\, sales and marketing strategies\, intellectual property\, choosing 
 the right legal entity\, business planning\, and incorporating AI into 
 business operations. Participants will also learn about revenue-readiness 
 software and discover support programs\, resources\, and organizations 
 available to help entrepreneurs launch and grow.\n\nThis program is 
 designed for aspiring entrepreneurs\, new business owners\, veterans\, and 
 anyone interested in learning more about the process of turning a business 
 idea into a sustainable venture. No prior business experience is 
 required.\n
LOCATION:Bloomfield - Conference Room\, Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10270-17601678
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/bloomfield/Boots2Business
END:VEVENT
